(7149475, 1095895, 102278, '<td valign="top">Lovely, got a 7 from me. Particularly interesting to see because i''m contemplating getting the DP Merrill 3 (and maybe the 1 to pair it with). I used to have the original DP 1 years ago and really liked it so have an idea of their operational limitations and also the image quality. These new Merrils look like amazing cameras.</td>', 'Lovely, got a 7 from me. Particularly interesting to see because i''m contemplating getting the DP Merrill 3 (and maybe the 1 to pair it with). I used to have the original DP 1 years ago and really liked it so have an idea of their operational limitations and also the image quality. These new Merrils look like amazing cameras.', '2013-12-30 12:23:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7149478, 1095950, 138630, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by streetpigeon:</b></div><hr/><i> Under-appreciated, in my opinion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks - I kind of thought so, too LOL</td>', 'Originally posted by streetpigeon: Under-appreciated, in my opinion.   Thanks - I kind of thought so, too LOL', '2013-12-30 12:26:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7149515, 1095895, 25024, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rooum:</b></div><hr/><i> Lovely, got a 7 from me. Particularly interesting to see because i''m contemplating getting the DP Merrill 3 (and maybe the 1 to pair it with). I used to have the original DP 1 years ago and really liked it so have an idea of their operational limitations and also the image quality. These new Merrils look like amazing cameras. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Do not hesitate in getting one Clive, they are quite simply stunning, but do be prepared to put up with the cameras many foibles and really slow down your image making but in my eyes that''s no bad thing. As for the Merrill 1 that''s exactly what I intend to do, once I have one I am seriously contemplating getting rid of the rest of my gear I am enjoying using this camera so much!<br/> <br/>Thank you everyone else for your positive comments.</td>', 'Originally posted by rooum: Lovely, got a 7 from me. Particularly interesting to see because i''m contemplating getting the DP Merrill 3 (and maybe the 1 to pair it with). I used to have the original DP 1 years ago and really liked it so have an idea of their operational limitations and also the image quality. These new Merrils look like amazing cameras.   Do not hesitate in getting one Clive, they are quite simply stunning, but do be prepared to put up with the cameras many foibles and really slow down your image making but in my eyes that''s no bad thing. As for the Merrill 1 that''s exactly what I intend to do, once I have one I am seriously contemplating getting rid of the rest of my gear I am enjoying using this camera so much! Thank you everyone else for your positive comments.', '2013-12-30 13:29:52.000000', NULL, 0),
